vent": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_015UoqRDzBKtGdVpD9RR7JnU", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54011, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015UoqRDzBKtGdVpD9RR7JnU", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55387, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Gfj8ywWRdBfF94cJBHEziF", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55687, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Gfj8ywWRdBfF94cJBHEziF", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55687, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Gfj8ywWRdBfF94cJBHEziF", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60090, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for it.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The bad v2.3.1 and the release before it, v2.3.1-rc, were both unhealthy.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, which left the other two regions on v2.3.1. I retried and it completed.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. The service is passing health checks, and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so there's only one incident and one page.\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the first attempt that stopped partway), the current state, and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n  - Find out what caused the error that stopped the first rollback attempt.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AtubBenvdLNiUKJ9X1Woqy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01MjtW9w2USdyq3eHWneTkns", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01NcPHi5Yr1Xk1CqKG5f1K9D", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014vDwaJx8MxQKGfNGKbtn8M", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I'm retrying.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018RYsoWAuDVJE637eW5BtsZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WejhQdR95QHheqG4hS3ype", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BRii23A9Y1zuJqtACiEEWt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015UoqRDzBKtGdVpD9RR7JnU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy (v2.3.1), checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west; the service is healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Gfj8ywWRdBfF94cJBHEziF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for it.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The bad v2.3.1 and the release before it, v2.3.1-rc, were both unhealthy.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, which left the other two regions on v2.3.1. I retried and it completed.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. The service is passing health checks, and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so there's only one incident and one page.\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the first attempt that stopped partway), the current state, and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n  - Find out what caused the error that stopped the first rollback attempt.", "type": "text"}]}]}